From c62fd337bbd0b30e8965c9c0fcc757bc12d37542 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Casati <diego.casati@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:44:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] ath12k: add WCN7850 support on FreeBSD

Make the WCN7850 (hw2.0, PCI) work through LinuxKPI.  All changes to the
vendor sources are under #if defined(__FreeBSD__) with the Linux code
kept in the #else branch, so the vendor diff is additive and future
imports stay mergeable.  New conditionals on CONFIG_OF and
CONFIG_ATH12K_AHB apply only to FreeBSD.

- qmi, mhi: use the stock qmi_handle_init() on the LinuxKPI QMI/QRTR
  implementation; deinit keeps the handle if LinuxKPI retains it.
- dp: track DMA ownership of the data path so that teardown after a
  failed or partial start never frees memory the device may still
  write.  Validate the CMEM page-table layout (dp_cc.h).
- wmi, htc, ce, pci, mhi: avoid void pointer arithmetic (the kernel
  is built with -Wpointer-arith), FreeBSD interrupt dispatch, and
  init, teardown and error-path state tracking.
- reg: support strict self-managed regulatory.  Apply the
  hw.ath12k.country tunable before the boot regd is published.  Accept
  NO_IR and radar channels in the strict channel list, and 5 GHz rules
  up to 80 MHz.  Skip the 6 GHz regd rebuild on authorize.
- The requested boot country is logged at ATH12K_DBG_REG instead of
  info.
- Declare MODULE_VERSION and MODULE_DEPEND on linuxkpi and
  linuxkpi_wlan (and lindebugfs with ATH12K_DEBUGFS), so kldload
  resolves them on kernels where they are modules.

Tested on WCN7850 hw2.0 with WPA2-PSK on 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz (VHT80).

Signed-off-by: Diego Casati <diego.casati@gmail.com>
